<section class="lab-hero" aria-labelledby="lab-title">
  <h1 id="lab-title">Compare what the tools actually returned.</h1>
  <p>Paste one prompt and the visible outputs. The lab measures structure, source links, and literal coverage—never hidden reasoning.</p>
</section>

<section class="ai-lab" id="compare" aria-labelledby="lab-workspace-title">
  <h2 class="visually-hidden" id="lab-workspace-title">AI output comparison workspace</h2>
  <form id="ai-lab-form" autocomplete="off">
    <div class="lab-setup">
      <h2>1. Shared setup</h2>
      <label for="lab-prompt">Prompt (shared)</label>
      <textarea id="lab-prompt" maxlength="4000" required placeholder="Paste the exact prompt used in each tool..."></textarea>
      <div class="field-meta"><span>Keep tool settings and research modes consistent where possible.</span><output id="lab-prompt-count" for="lab-prompt">0 / 4000</output></div>

      <label for="lab-criteria">Criteria <span>(optional)</span></label>
      <textarea id="lab-criteria" maxlength="1200" placeholder="One criterion per line, for example:&#10;Current primary sources&#10;Limitations&#10;Concrete next step"></textarea>
      <div class="field-meta"><span>Literal coverage is mechanical, not a quality score.</span><output id="lab-criteria-count" for="lab-criteria">0 / 1200</output></div>

      <p class="lab-privacy">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="5" y="10" width="14" height="11" rx="2" /><path d="M8 10V7a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v3" /></svg>
        Browser-local. Nothing is sent or retained. Do not paste confidential material.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="lab-outputs">
      <div class="lab-output-heading"><h2>2. Visible outputs</h2><p>Use final answer text only. Rename a column for Perplexity or another tool.</p></div>
      <div class="lab-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="AI output editors">
        <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="lab-panel-0" data-lab-tab="0">ChatGPT</button>
        <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="lab-panel-1" data-lab-tab="1">Claude</button>
        <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="lab-panel-2" data-lab-tab="2">Gemini</button>
      </div>
      <div class="lab-output-grid">
        {[
          ["ChatGPT", 0],
          ["Claude", 1],
          ["Gemini", 2],
        ].map(([name, index]) => (
          <section class:list={["lab-output-panel", { "is-active": index === 0 }]} id={`lab-panel-${index}`} data-lab-panel={index} role="tabpanel">
            <label for={`lab-name-${index}`}>Tool name</label>
            <input id={`lab-name-${index}`} data-lab-name={index} type="text" maxlength="40" value={name} />
            <label for={`lab-output-${index}`}>Output <span>(visible text only)</span></label>
            <textarea id={`lab-output-${index}`} data-lab-output={index} maxlength="24000" placeholder={`Paste the visible output from ${name}...`}></textarea>
            <output class="lab-output-count" data-lab-output-count={index}>0 / 24000</output>
          </section>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="lab-submit-row">
        <button class="primary-button" type="submit">Compare outputs</button>
        <output id="lab-form-status" aria-live="polite"></output>
      </div>
    </div>
  </form>
</section>

<section class="lab-results" id="lab-results" aria-labelledby="lab-results-title" hidden>
  <header>
    <div><p class="mono-label">Observable text only</p><h2 id="lab-results-title">Comparison results</h2></div>
    <div class="lab-result-actions"><button type="button" id="lab-reset">Reset</button><button type="button" id="lab-export">Export JSON</button></div>
  </header>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="lab-metric-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Measure</th><th data-result-name="0">ChatGPT</th><th data-result-name="1">Claude</th><th data-result-name="2">Gemini</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Words</th><td data-metric="words" data-tool="0">—</td><td data-metric="words" data-tool="1">—</td><td data-metric="words" data-tool="2">—</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Markdown headings</th><td data-metric="headings" data-tool="0">—</td><td data-metric="headings" data-tool="1">—</td><td data-metric="headings" data-tool="2">—</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">List items</th><td data-metric="lists" data-tool="0">—</td><td data-metric="lists" data-tool="1">—</td><td data-metric="lists" data-tool="2">—</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Unique source links</th><td data-metric="links" data-tool="0">—</td><td data-metric="links" data-tool="1">—</td><td data-metric="links" data-tool="2">—</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Literal criteria</th><td data-metric="criteria" data-tool="0">—</td><td data-metric="criteria" data-tool="1">—</td><td data-metric="criteria" data-tool="2">—</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <div class="visible-differences">
    <h3>Visible differences</h3>
    <ul id="lab-differences"></ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="lab-method" id="how-comparison-works" aria-labelledby="lab-method-title">
  <div><h2 id="lab-method-title">What this comparison can prove</h2><p>It gives you a reproducible description of the pasted text. Factual review still happens against current primary sources.</p></div>
  <dl>
    <div><dt>Words</dt><dd>Unicode word-like tokens in the visible answer.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Headings</dt><dd>Lines written as Markdown headings with <code>#</code>.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Source links</dt><dd>Unique explicit HTTP or HTTPS URLs.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Literal criteria</dt><dd>A criterion counts when at least half of its non-trivial words appear. This can miss good paraphrases and reward repetition.</dd></div>
  </dl>
  <p class="lab-boundary">The lab does not call any provider API, name a winner, verify claims, infer private queries, or expose chain of thought.</p>
  <a class="text-link" href="/blog/how-to-compare-ai-answers-without-guessing/">Read the comparison protocol <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
</section>

